@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# Optional Xray runtime
+
+Place the Android AAR built from the official `XTLS/libXray` project here as `libXray.aar`.
+The Gradle module includes local JAR/AAR files from this directory. The source archive does not bundle a prebuilt native core.
+
+From a development machine with network access, Go, Python 3, Android SDK/NDK and the required gomobile toolchain, run:
+
+```sh
+LIBXRAY_REF=<reviewed-tag-or-commit> ./tools/build-libxray-aar.sh
+```
+
+The script prints the exact source revision and SHA-256 of the output. Review upstream changes and license notices before choosing a revision; do not blindly use a moving branch for a release. The bridge is intentionally reflective because the generated Java package can vary by gomobile build. Runtime start-up will report a missing AAR instead of claiming the tunnel is active.
