@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# Xray / VLESS integration status
+
+## Included in this source archive
+
+- VLESS share-link parsing and Xray JSON generation for TCP, WebSocket, gRPC, HTTP, HTTPUpgrade and XHTTP/SplitHTTP profiles, with `none`, TLS and supported Reality combinations.
+- Validation for UUID, port, Reality public key/short ID, unsupported transports, malformed XHTTP `extra`, and VLESS `flow` combinations. TLS certificate verification remains enabled.
+- App-private storage for one imported profile, plus TV-friendly import, start, stop and remove controls in Network settings.
+- A reflective bridge to the official XTLS/libXray `Invoke` API. It checks the native response and fails clearly when the AAR is missing.
+- Restoration of the previous SmartTube proxy preferences and player data-source setting after stopping the tunnel.
+- SponsorBlock remains part of the original SmartTube source and was not removed.
+
+## What is not finished or verified
+
+**This archive is source/preparation work, not a ready-to-install APK.** No APK was built in this environment. The Android SDK and the `SharedModules` / `MediaServiceCore` Git submodules are missing, and Gradle could not be downloaded because outbound DNS/network access failed. The native `common/libs/libXray.aar` is also not bundled.
+
+Until the AAR is built, placed at `common/libs/libXray.aar`, and included in a successful Android build, the VLESS start action will report that the core is unavailable. Use `tools/build-libxray-aar.sh` on a machine with Git, Python 3, Go, Android SDK/NDK, gomobile prerequisites and network access. Review and record the upstream revision and artifact hash before distributing a build.
+
+Even with the AAR, this implementation routes only SmartTube network clients that honor the configured app proxy. It is **not** an Android `VpnService` and does not guarantee that Cronet or every media/network path is proxied. The full app build, native startup, TLS/Reality profiles, playback, SponsorBlock, proxy restoration and Android TV behavior still need device-level testing.
+
+## Security notes
+
+- TLS verification is enabled (`allowInsecure: false`).
+- The SOCKS inbound binds to `127.0.0.1:10808`, not the LAN.
+- VLESS share links contain credentials. They are stored in app-private preferences and must not be logged, sent to analytics, or synced. App-private preferences are not hardware-backed encrypted storage.
+- Do not publish a release signed with someone else's signing key.
+
+## Build steps
+
+On a development computer with a compatible JDK, Android SDK/build-tools and network access:
+
+```sh
+./tools/prepare-build.sh
+./tools/build-libxray-aar.sh
+./tools/build-tv-debug.sh
+```
+
+The legacy SmartTube revision warns that OpenJDK 14 or older is required. Verify compatibility with the exact installed Android Gradle Plugin and SDK before building. The libXray build script prints the checked-out upstream revision and SHA-256 of the resulting AAR; retain both with release artifacts.
+
+## Automated build workflow
+
+The source archive includes `.github/workflows/build-fork-apk.yml`. In a GitHub repository under your control, run **Actions → Build SmartTube VLESS fork → Run workflow**. On success, download the `smarttube-vless-fork-debug` artifact, which contains the debug APK, the libXray AAR, and checksums. The workflow has not been run from this environment; its success and the actual device behavior remain unverified until a remote run and TV-device test complete.
diff -ruN smarttube_baseline/SmartTube-master/tools/build-libxray-aar.sh smarttube_work/SmartTube-master/tools/build-libxray-aar.sh
--- smarttube_baseline/SmartTube-master/tools/build-libxray-aar.sh	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ smarttube_work/SmartTube-master/tools/build-libxray-aar.sh	2026-10-29 16:26:58.766342653 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -euo pipefail
+
+# Build the official XTLS/libXray Android AAR and copy it into SmartTube's local module libs.
+# Requires Git, Python 3, Go, Android SDK/NDK, gomobile prerequisites, and network access.
+ROOT="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)"
+WORK="${LIBXRAY_WORKDIR:-$ROOT/.work/libXray}"
+REF="${LIBXRAY_REF:-main}"
+
+if ! command -v git >/dev/null 2>&1 || ! command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+  echo "ERROR: git and python3 are required" >&2
+  exit 2
+fi
+if ! command -v go >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+  echo "ERROR: Go is required to build libXray" >&2
+  exit 2
+fi
+
+mkdir -p "$(dirname "$WORK")"
+if [ ! -d "$WORK/.git" ]; then
+  git clone https://github.com/XTLS/libXray.git "$WORK"
+fi
+git -C "$WORK" fetch --tags origin
+git -C "$WORK" checkout "$REF"
+echo "Building XTLS/libXray revision: $(git -C "$WORK" rev-parse HEAD)"
+
+(
+  cd "$WORK"
+  python3 build/main.py android
+)
+
+AAR="$(find "$WORK" -type f -name '*.aar' -not -path '*/.git/*' -printf '%T@ %p\n' | sort -nr | head -n1 | cut -d' ' -f2-)"
+if [ -z "${AAR:-}" ] || [ ! -f "$AAR" ]; then
+  echo "ERROR: build completed without an AAR artifact; inspect libXray build output" >&2
+  exit 3
+fi
+mkdir -p "$ROOT/common/libs"
+cp "$AAR" "$ROOT/common/libs/libXray.aar"
+sha256sum "$ROOT/common/libs/libXray.aar"
+echo "Copied libXray AAR to common/libs/libXray.aar"
+echo "Verify its license, source revision and supported ABIs before distributing a build."
